FRICTION_KINDS = ("refused", "broken-tool", "flaky-check", "unclear-rule", "slow", "other")
FRICTION_HELP = """powos friction - what got in the way, logged where it gets fixed for good

Hit friction (a refusal, a broken or flaky tool, an unclear rule, something slow)? Log it BEFORE you work
around it. The same area + kind + title counts up (no duplicates); the board sweeper's digest to the
coordinator lists new and recurring ones by count, and the top ones become permanent fixes.

  powos friction add --area AREA --kind KIND "<title: what happened, one line>"
                     --repro "<how to make it happen again: the command or the steps>"
                     [--details TEXT | --details -]   the whole story (stdin with -): what you did, what
                                                      you saw, what you expected, how you got around it
                     [--evidence PATH] [--by ROLE]
          KIND: refused | broken-tool | flaky-check | unclear-rule | slow | other
          AREA: what it's in - ship, gate, verify, board, comms, permissions, worktree, phone, apk, ...
          --repro is required: "none: <why it can't be reproduced>" when there's really no way.
          --fixed SHA: logging one that's already fixed (a record of it; it reopens if it comes back).
  powos friction list [--all] [--fixed] [--area A] [--id ID ...] [--json]   open ones, most frequent first
                     --id: just these ids (repeatable) - a cluster's status in one call, not the whole dump
  powos friction show <id>                     one, whole (details, repro, evidence)
  powos friction fix <id> --commit SHA [--note TEXT]   fixed for good; logged again later, it reopens

Tools log their own: a ship refusal or failure (ship.sh), a shell gate failure under Mac load (gate.sh),
an INVALID or SKIPPED phone check (queue.sh), a permission refusal of an agent's tool call (powos-agentsd).
Off the phone (the Mac): python3 lib/ai/agents/powos-agents-cli friction ...  (tools/agents/friction).
"""


def friction_cmd(argv):
